 174:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     Callbacks can be registered / unregistered in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY state only.
 175:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     Exception done MspInit / MspDeInit that can be registered / unregistered
 176:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY or HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET state,
 177:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     thus registered(user) MspInit / DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init / DeInit.
 178:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 179:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****       using HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() before calling DeInit or Init function.
